{"diagnosis": "256-word NOP fetch expects aligned progress with no trap but trace shows TRAP: cpu trap asserted with tohost FAIL 0xdead vs expected PASS/no-trap. Trace window is sparse/unclear (only CYCLES=2009, no PC/opcode), so exact mis-decode cycle cannot be pinned. Root cause in excerpt picorv32.v:1446 `decoder_trigger <= mem_do_rinst || mem_done` spuriously re-triggers decoder on mem_done, corrupting fetch alignment and causing illegal trap; grounding picosoc/picosoc.v:146 cpu with picosoc/picosoc.v:149-155 mem_valid/mem_ready path, trace wins.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -1446,7 +1446,7 @@
 		decoder_trigger <= mem_do_rinst || mem_done;
 		decoder_trigger_q <= decoder_trigger;
 		decoder_pseudo_trigger <= 0;
 		decoder_pseudo_trigger_q <= decoder_pseudo_trigger;
 		do_waitirq <= 0;

 		trace_valid <= 0;
+ 		decoder_trigger <= mem_do_rinst;
", "expected": "tohost PASS with no TRAP: cpu trap asserted, checksum != c2a7a4d6295484feeb9ec1ea9381732b8e39a7ccd1997c7d70f6454da2fb4659"}

